        }
      }
    },
    "Tailscale handles sign-in in your browser; SparkPilot does not ask for your account password.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tailscale handles sign-in in your browser; SparkPilot does not ask for your account password."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tailscale in the App Store": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tailscale in the App Store"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tailscale is a private network between your own devices. It is built on WireGuard, a modern encryption protocol, so your devices talk to each other over encrypted connections, directly when possible or through a relay when needed.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tailscale is a private network between your own devices. It is built on WireGuard, a modern encryption protocol, so your devices talk to each other over encrypted connections, directly when possible or through a relay when needed."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tailscale is a separate app and service from Tailscale Inc.; it manages your account and VPN connection, while SparkPilot checks access to your Spark.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tailscale is a separate app and service from Tailscale Inc.; it manages your account and VPN connection, while SparkPilot checks access to your Spark."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tailscale is installed and running on your Spark, waiting to be signed in: finishing that sign-in later would put the Spark on your tailnet. To undo it, run `sudo tailscale logout` then `sudo systemctl disable --now tailscaled` on the Spark.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tailscale is installed and running on your Spark, waiting to be signed in: finishing that sign-in later would put the Spark on your tailnet. To undo it, run `sudo tailscale logout` then `sudo systemctl disable --now tailscaled` on the Spark."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tailscale is installed on your Spark and stopped, so the Spark is not on your tailnet.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tailscale is installed on your Spark and stopped, so the Spark is not on your tailnet."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tailscale is not installed on your Spark, so the attempt left nothing behind.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tailscale is not installed on your Spark, so the attempt left nothing behind."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tailscale is optional; on your home network, SparkPilot can connect directly.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tailscale is optional; on your home network, SparkPilot can connect directly."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tailscale is signed in and running on your Spark, so the Spark is on your tailnet even though SparkPilot did not record the route. To undo it, run `sudo tailscale logout` then `sudo systemctl disable --now tailscaled` on the Spark.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tailscale is signed in and running on your Spark, so the Spark is on your tailnet even though SparkPilot did not record the route. To undo it, run `sudo tailscale logout` then `sudo systemctl disable --now tailscaled` on the Spark."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tailscale is signed in on your Spark and waiting for your tailnet's admin to approve it, and it joins as soon as they do. To undo it, run `sudo tailscale logout` then `sudo systemctl disable --now tailscaled` on the Spark.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tailscale is signed in on your Spark and waiting for your tailnet's admin to approve it, and it joins as soon as they do. To undo it, run `sudo tailscale logout` then `sudo systemctl disable --now tailscaled` on the Spark."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tailscale is signed in, but the route is not answering yet": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tailscale is signed in, but the route is not answering yet"
